Abstract
.ft
.ps
.ti 3
.sp 1
I will develop a user friendly computer program to aid writers in
the prewriting process. My research of prewriting heuristics will come 
primarily from composition journals such as \fICollege Composition 
and Communication\fR and \fICollege English\fR, with
additional information coming from a survey of existing prewriting software,
instructional texts, surveys
and interviews with writing instructors and composition experts.
I will use the information from the surveys and interviews to see
what preparation writing instructors use before they write a text as well as
and how they teach their students to prewrite.  I will write the prewriting 
program to fit the instructors' and students' needs.  The
software will be assessed and go through a series of tests
before I make it available to the English
Department's account on the UNIX/Local Area Network of Virginia Commonwealth University where writers can access the
program.  The software
will then be released for use by faculty, English 101 classes,
individual students, and both beginning and advanced writers.
.sp 2
.ft HB
.ps 12
Background
.ft
.sp 1
.ps
.ti 3
Composing is comprised of several recursive processes: prewriting, drafting, and
revision.  Prewriting is the process in which writers develop and
focus their ideas for texts, but often, heuristics for such processes are
difficult for students to use.  For example, two heuristics designed to
help writers in the prewriting process are the "pentad,"
developed by Kenneth Burke, and the "particle/wave/field"
heuristic, developed by Richard Young, Kenneth Pike, and Alton
Becker.  Both of these heuristics have several complicated
sequences to follow, along with jargon that makes them difficult for
the beginning writer to understand without additional
instructions from a professor.  A prewriting program would
provide the "translation" of a heuristic while the computer would
allow the writer access to the program.
.ti 3
The English Department of Virginia Commonwealth University uses
a UNIX/LAN with word processing software such as
Word Perfect, VI Text Editor and Writer's Workbench to help both
beginning and advanced writers enter and revise texts.  A
prewriting program installed  on the system  would allow all
English students, and all writers who have access to the Hibbs
computer, to develop their ideas through the use of the
prewriting program.  Based on the research I have done,  few user friendly
prewriting programs that aid the writer through the prewriting process are
available.
.ft HB
.ps 12
.sp 2
Goals
.ft
.ps
.sp 1
Through this project I hope to 
.sp 1
.BL 2
.LI
gain an understanding of composition theory 
.LI
assess departmental and classroom prewriting needs 
.LI
gain a practical knowledge of prewriting through surveys and interviews with
professional writers and writing instructors
.LI
