.LE
.ti 3
I have begun research of prewriting heuristics and the software
available for computer assisted instruction (CAI) of prewriting
and have assessed some departmental needs through informal
interviews with the Dr. Elizabeth Hodges, Director of the Composition program
and Writing/Computer Center and Michael Keller,
Computer Coordinator of the Center.
.ti 3
I am a weekly volunteer at the English Writing/Computer Center
and help beginning writers with problems that they have
with using the computer.
.ti 3
I am currently developing a survey for writing instructors (see "Sample
Survey" attached to \fBPreparation\fR sheet).
.sp 2
.ft HB
.ps 12
Procedures
.ft R
.ps 
.sp1
.BL 3
.LI
Research published heuristics in composition journals and instructional texts
.LI
Contact textbook publishers and compile a list of available college level
prewriting software 
.LI
Purchase five prewriting programs to review
.LI
Survey (see "Sample Survey") and interview selected
writing instructors at Virginia Commonwealth University,
including Director of the English Department, Dr. James Kinney,
and Dr. Elizabeth Hodges.
.LI
Conduct telephone interviews with professional writers,
composition experts, and composition directors at other schools.  Each
interview should take about a half of an hour.
.LI
Study survey and interview responses and develop a
practical prewriting heuristic and computer program based on research and responses. 
.LI
Test a completed draft with five instructors to see if the heuristic is
practical for in class use.  Take comments from the instructors and adjust
the heuristic and/or program to respond to their problems.
.LI
Test instructors revision on two Composition and Rhetoric classes.  As the
student exits the program he will be asked to do an on-line evaluation.   The
results will be sent to me electronically so that I can adjust the software to
help them understand the heuristic and the computer program. The test will be
repeated until beginning writers are able to use the program for the first
time without extra assistance. 
.LI
The English department allows students and instructors to access a help
program known as TUTOR through a special account on the UNIX/LAN.  The program
will be placed in the account where the staff and students can access it.
.LI
Through a special program, I will make a record of everyone who accesses the program
and determine what kind of writers use the program most, 
recording English 101 and 102 accounts and graduate accounts
separately from other accounts which may use the program.
.LE
.sp2
.bp
.ft HB
.ps 12
Originality
.sp 1
.ft R
.ps
.ti 3
Dr. Elizabeth Hodges has suggested that a prewriting program be
written for the English Department.  I have taken her suggestion
and begun the research for the project and I have determined the
procedure for creating the program.  The English Department
does not have access to a prewriting program, and I am eager to
create a practical software package that can be used by both
beginning and professional writers.
.ti 3
I am interested in surveying
and interviewing professional writers who teach writing to see if they use the same
prewriting techniques that they teach or if their ways of teaching prewriting
differ from what textbooks and journals suggest.  I will then need to determine what
method is the most practical for all writers. 
.sp 2
.ft HB
.ps 12
Personal Value
.ft R
.ps 
.ti 3
.sp 1
I am interested in writing and I have enjoyed computing as a
hobby.  I have assisted in the development of a program called
TUTOR that is in use in on the computers that the English
Department uses.  The research involved in developing an easy to
understand computer/prewriting heuristic will expand my
knowledge of the writing process and  will help me become a better
writer and computer programmer.  As a person who is constantly
trying to clarify and develop ideas for
my writing, I see how this computer program can work for my own
benefit and for the benefit of people like myself who want to
write well.

